  "secondDefensible": "B — Chen's original 1976 ER paper formalises an attribute as a function from the entity set into a value set (E -> V); only Elmasri & Navathe use the power set P(V), and Silberschatz gives no function-based definition at all.",
  "issue": "The stem says only 'in the ER model' and 'formally defined as a function', but the answer depends entirely on which text's formalisation is meant: E&N give A : E -> P(V) (the key), Chen gives E -> V (option B). The stem should name the E&N convention, or hint that the definition must accommodate multivalued and null-valued attributes."
